==English==

===Etymology===
From the the expression "I'd {{m|en|rather}}" (meaning "I would prefer to") often pronounced "I druther" in some dialects.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/ˈdɹʌðɚz/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-druthers.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-plural noun}}

# {{lb|en|US|informal|often [[jocular]]}} [[wish|Wishes]], [[preference]]s, or [[way]]s.
#: ''If I had my '''druthers''' I’d eat in a restaurant every night of the week.''
#* '''1929''', Harry McClintock, [https://archive.org/details/HarrymacMcclintock-IfIHadMyDruthers1929 "If I Had My Druthers"]
#*: "If I had my '''druthers''', I would not be a king. I'd '''druther''' be just what I am than any other thing."
#* {{quote-text|lang=en|year=1950|author=Alice Walworth Graham|title=The Natchez Woman|passage="If you had your '''druthers'''—" Old Lew was always saying, "If I had my '''druthers''', gimme one of them there Shevrolics."}}
#* {{quote-text|lang=en|year=1957|author=Society of Arts and Crafts|title=Theatre Arts|volume=41|page=29|passage="If I had my '''druthers'''," he informs us, "I'druther be myself — not because I'm anythin' special, just because it's convenient."}}
#* {{quote-text|lang=en|year=1977|author=Carole Mayhall|title=From the Heart of a Woman|passage=If I'd had my "'''druthers'''," our engagement would not have been two and one half years long. But schooling made our '''druthers''' invalid.}}
#* {{quote-text|lang=en|year=1993|author=Les Claypool|title=DMV|passage=If I had my "'''druthers'''," I'd screw a chimpanzee. Call it, pointless.}}

====Usage notes====
* The singular form "druther" is used with the same meaning, but much more rarely.

* The noun "druthers" is sometimes used in conjunction with the verb "druther" for increased comic effect.
*: ''If I've got my '''druthers''', I'd '''druther''' not.''
*: or, alternatively,
*: ''If I've got my '''druthers''', I '''druther''' not.''
: This double formation was popularized by the American cartoonist [[w:Al Capp|Al Capp]] (1909-1979) in the long-running ''[[w:Li'l Abner|Li'l Abner]]'' comic strip and was also featured in the song "If I Had my Druthers" in ''[[w:Li'l Abner (musical)|Li'l Abner: The Musical]]'' (1956).

